[32m+[m[32m# Nexus LAN TEST mode (development only, plain HTTP)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLets Barcode Auto Print on another PC reach Nexus on the development PC. **Never** use this on a public network or in[m
[32m+[m[32mproduction: production is HTTPS only (see `DEPLOYMENT.md`) and Django refuses `NEXUS_LAN_TEST_MODE` when `DJANGO_DEBUG=False`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Root cause of `NEXUS_UNREACHABLE` (found 2026-11-10)[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Nothing was listening on port 8001 (the server was not running).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. `runserver` defaulted to `127.0.0.1`, so even when running it was invisible to other PCs.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. `ALLOWED_HOSTS` held only `localhost,127.0.0.1`, so a request to `http://<LAN IP>:8001` would have been refused (HTTP 400).[m
[32m+[m[32m4. The dev PC's DHCP address moved from 192.168.1.15 to 192.168.1.13, so PRN's saved URL pointed at a dead address.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Configure (backend/.env, git-ignored)[m
[32m+[m[32m    DJANGO_DEBUG=True[m
[32m+[m[32m    NEXUS_LAN_TEST_MODE=True[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn this mode `runserver` binds `0.0.0.0:8001` and this PC's private LAN IPs are added to `ALLOWED_HOSTS` automatically[m
[32m+[m[32m(no wildcard), so a changed DHCP address needs no edit. Better still, give the PC a DHCP reservation / static IP.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Start[m
[32m+[m[32m    cd D:\SaiInfosysNexus\backend[m
[32m+[m[32m    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe manage.py runserver --noreload[m
